│ Okay, let’s address this. Based on the       │
│ provided context and the repeated API        │
│ failures, the core issue seems to be that    │
│ Sphinx is incorrectly resolving unqualified  │
│ names (like 'A') in xref definitions. It     │
│ appears to be defaulting to resolving them   │
│ within the current module instead of the     │
│ intended sub-module. The fix involves        │
│ explicitly specifying the module prefix in   │
│ the xref definitions.                        │
│                                              │
│ Reasoning:                                   │
│                                              │
│ The problem stems from Sphinx’s default      │
│ behavior when encountering an unqualified    │
│ name in a cross-reference. It searches for   │
│ the name within the current module and its   │
│ parent modules. To resolve this, we need to  │
│ ensure that the xref definitions explicitly  │
│ specify the correct module for each class    │
│ and function. This will force Sphinx to      │
│ resolve the xrefs to the intended            │
│ sub-module.                                  │
│                                              │
